                        "entry_id": "f882f4f9-a7b9-3ef5-a5ee-34ce4cc33410",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chaotic, disorganised or mismanaged."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Commonwealth",
                            "Ireland",
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "781a211f-4565-436b-9914-2a1c44fcb606",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "[O]ne must admit there were those among us who were somewhat on the shambolic side."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "282ff4c9-7a3d-4402-afc7-b0409776ced4",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "He said his club had coined a new word 'Shambolic,' which meant spending more time watching the weather than playing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a14d0dbb-4c2c-4c8a-b4e9-b731050c8518",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "The precautionary principle is a culturally framed concept that takes its cue from changing social conceptions about the appropriate roles of science, economics, ethics, politics and the law in pro-active environmental protection and management. As this book will reveal, it is a rather shambolic concept, muddled in policy advice and subject to the whims of international diplomacy and the unpredictable public mood over the true cost of sustainable living."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d625e15-b037-4a1e-abdd-6d15c97b14a4",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "The pub was empty of all but the most dedicated drinkers, shambolic figures huddled over bottles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0dab94cc-02e2-4585-802c-3959384e82f7",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "The shabby subterfuge surrounding Suez [the Suez Crisis], as much as its shambolic aftermath, have made it a symbol of the collapse of British global power in the post-war era."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "053da344-4e47-4f7a-8a25-2862f18294d4",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "During normal times, distribution of goods or services to over 7,000 islands [in the Philippines] is difficult, and the reality is that on a day-to-day basis, it's shambolic. There are too many examples of corruption and inefficiency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bb1e625-b8f8-4161-8b51-0650f3d046ab",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "New train introduction had become shambolic with extended delays - mainly due to repeated software issues, seriously late deliveries, and gauging problems."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71364213-1bfe-4138-952d-aea9ac74d317",
                                "sense_id": "d2dc323a-7f77-3906-990b-ddbbe65a99bb",
                                "text": "Donald Trump’s tax returns illustrate the profound inequities of the tax code and the shambolic state of federal enforcement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
